    "https://www.dbq.edu/CampusLife/StudentServicesResources/CareerServicesandCommunityEngagement": {
      "title": "Vocation, Career Services, & Community Engagement",
      "description": "Career Services and Community Engagement | University of Dubuque Skip Navigation Apply Visit Invest Heritage Center Payments Search Toggle Search Menu Quick Links Back MyCampus Login News and Events Calendar Event Requests Academic Calendar Charles C. Myers Library Bookstore Dining Services Directory Admission & Aid Back Admission & Aid Apply Now Schedule a Visit What Sets Us Apart Request Information Costs Financial Aid Spartans Ready Prospective Students Transfer Students Former UD Students Graduate Students LIFE - Adult Accelerated Degrees Veterans Housing Application Pay Admission Deposit Campus Life Back Campus Life Apply Now Visit Us Student Services & Resources Student Involvement Residence Life Student Guidelines Career Services News & Events Office of Technology Smeltzer-Kelly Student Health Center Campus Ministry Wendt Center Office of Student Life Safety and Security Academics Back Academics Apply Now MyUD LOGIN Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs UD Global / LIFE HyFlex Programs Theological Seminary Programs Academic Advising Academic Calendars Academic Success Center TRIO/SSS Library Office of the Registrar Special Learning Opportunities Office of Academic Affairs Seminary Back Seminary Apply Now About UDTS Schedule a Visit Academic Programs Special Programs Choosing a Program Faculty and Staff Lectures & Events Outreach & Connections Financial Aid Connect with Us Athletics Back Athletics Athletic Calendar Athletics Staff Directory Recreation Facilities Student Athlete Handbook Alumni & Investors Back Alumni & Investors Invest Now Update My Information The Momentum Campaign Alumni Events & Activities Alumni Awards & Recognition Giving to UD Impact Stories Alumni Perks & Benefits Alumni: Campus Visit UD News & Events Athletic Events Heritage Center Stay Connected Apply Visit Invest Heritage Center Payments Vocation, Career Services, & Community Engagement The University of Dubuque's Office of Vocation, Career Services, and Community Engagement is here to help students prepare for their chosen vocation and future endeavors. Whether you are exploring careers, looking for engagement opportunities, applying for an internship, or considering graduate school, we provide support for whatever phase you are on in your educational journey. Through consultations, virtual resources, and meaningful community connections, you will feel prepared for your next step. Your journey starts today! List of Services Below are several services our office can assist with. Appointments with our staff can be scheduled by emailing Career@dbq.edu . If what you are looking for is not listed below, please contact us at Career@dbq.edu to help get you started! Our office strives to prepare you to be competent in these career readiness areas from the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE): Career & Self Development Leadership Communicatrion Professionalism Critical Thinking Teamwork Technology ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ Support Us! Interested in making a donation to support our Food Share Co-op and/or Success Shop? Monetary donations can be accepted via check to: U niversity of Dubuque, Attn: Career Services, 2000 University Ave., Dubuque, IA Memo: Food Share or Success Shop Or check out our Amazon Wishlists here: Food Share Co-Op Wishlist Success Shop Wishlist Items will  be shipped directly to the University of Dubuque when you purchase via Amazon. Thank you so much for supporting student success! Resume and Cover Letter Development and Reviews Toggle Accordion Visibility Our staff is available to support you in the development and fine-tuning of your resume and cover letter as you prepare to apply for jobs, internships, and other opportunities. We offer individual consultations to ensure your resume is employer ready. We also collaborate with academic departments, student organizations, and athletic teams to provide presentations and workshops to help groups of students. Current students, schedule and appointment with us through WCOnline ! Mock Interviews Toggle Accordion Visibility Students have the opportunity to prepare for upcoming interviews through a simulated interview experience. Local and regional professionals donate their time to provide students with feedback on interview skills and a critique of the student's resume, including strengths and weaknesses. Mock Interviews Career Coaching Toggle Accordion Visibility Through a confidential setting either face-to-face or a virtual format, we provide support and assistance to students struggling to choose a major or career path. We'll spend time with you determining your overall goals and developing an action plan for exploring your options. Graduate or Professional School Preparation Toggle Accordion Visibility We can help review the application process, school/program selection, make recommendations and assess requirements identified by the school/program. We can also help with information regarding test preparation material and registration, if required through the application process. Graduate/Professional School Resources Career Fairs Toggle Accordion Visibility Follow us on social media and watch your email for opportunities to connect with employers through career fairs throughout the school year. Connect with Our Staff Emma Powell Coordinator of Student Engagement and Formation Email: ELPowell@dbq.edu Department: Student Life Office: 208 Peters Commons Helpful Links Internship Resources Job Search Resources Career Resources Community Service Opportunities Graduate School Resources Vocation and Civic Engagement Information for Employers Information for Faculty & Staff Information for Parents & Guardians 2000 University Ave. Dubuque IA, 52001 563.589.3000 Directory Safety & Security Reporting Hotline About UD Careers Jeanne Clery Act Title IX Map & Directions Apply My Campus Login Copyright 2021 University of Dubuque. All rights reserved. HEERF Reports Privacy Statement Accessibility Consumer Information Contact Facebook Instagram Twitter You Tube LinkedIn"
